252	/// is said of the file whose generator made it. One at code the PROGRAM wrote, which a hole carried
253	/// into the item — a field's rule, a body an annotation wraps — stands in the program's own file, its
254	/// spans counted from there; where the written item the generator stood on already says it, it is
255	/// that item's, said once. Its edits would write the template, never the program, and aren't offered.
256	fn made_finding(engine: QueryEngine, file: SourceFileAddress, at: int, f: LawFinding) -> LawFinding? {
